===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/typescript/cors-credentials-wildcard.yml
# Generated by forge from typescript/cors-credentials-wildcard (mode: forbid).
id: typescript/cors-credentials-wildcard
language: Tsx
severity: error
message: forge:typescript/cors-credentials-wildcard CORS with credentials true names its allowed origins. origin "*" is refused by browsers with credentials; origin true, or a function that returns the origin it is given (alone or with a ?? / || fallback, as an expression or a return), lets any site make credentialed requests. Covers cors (Express), hono/cors, @fastify/cors and Nest's enableCors.
files:
  - packages/core/**
rule:
  kind: call_expression
  any:
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            kind: member_expression
            has:
              field: property
              regex: ^register$
        - has:
            field: arguments
            all:
              - has:
                  nthChild: 1
                  pattern: $PLUGIN
              - has:
                  nthChild: 2
                  matches: any-origin-with-credentials
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            kind: member_expression
            all:
              - has:
                  field: object
                  pattern: $APP
              - has:
                  field: property
                  regex: ^enableCors$
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild: 1
              matches: any-origin-with-credentials
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            kind: member_expression
            all:
              - has:
                  field: object
                  pattern: $NEST
              - has:
                  field: property
                  regex: ^create$
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild: 2
              kind: object
              has:
                kind: pair
                all:
                  - has:
                      field: key
                      regex: ^["']?cors["']?$
                  - has:
                      field: value
                      matches: any-origin-with-credentials
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            pattern: $CORS
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild: 1
              matches: any-origin-with-credentials
utils:
  any-origin-with-credentials:
    kind: object
    all:
      - has:
          kind: pair
          all:
            - has:
                field: key
                regex: ^["']?credentials["']?$
            - has:
                field: value
                kind: "true"
      - has:
          kind: pair
          all:
            - has:
                field: key
                regex: ^["']?origin["']?$
            - has:
                field: value
                any:
                  - regex: ^["']\*["']$
                  - kind: "true"
                  - all:
                      - any:
                          - kind: arrow_function
                          - kind: function_expression
                      - any:
                          - has:
                              field: parameter
                              pattern: $O
                          - has:
                              field: parameters
                              has:
                                nthChild: 1
                                has:
                                  field: pattern
                                  pattern: $O
                      - any:
                          - has:
                              field: body
                              any:
                                - pattern: $O
                                - pattern: $O ?? $D
                                - pattern: $O || $D
                                - pattern: ($O)
                          - has:
                              field: body
                              kind: statement_block
                              has:
                                stopBy: end
                                kind: return_statement
                                has:
                                  any:
                                    - pattern: $O
                                    - pattern: $O ?? $D
                                    - pattern: $O || $D
metadata:
  forge_where:
    CORS:
      declared:
        - package: cors
        - package: hono
          name: cors
    PLUGIN:
      declared:
        package: "@fastify/cors"
    APP:
      type:
        package: "@nestjs/common"
        name: INestApplication
    NEST:
      declared:
        package: "@nestjs/core"
        name: NestFactory

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/typescript/no-double-assertion.yml
# Generated by forge from typescript/no-double-assertion (mode: forbid).
id: typescript/no-double-assertion
language: Tsx
severity: error
message: forge:typescript/no-double-assertion No double type assertions (x as unknown as T). Parse with a schema or narrow with a type guard.
files:
  - packages/core/**
rule:
  any:
    - pattern: $X as unknown as $T
    - pattern: $X as any as $T

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/typescript/no-dynamic-regexp.yml
# Generated by forge from typescript/no-dynamic-regexp (mode: advise).
id: typescript/no-dynamic-regexp
language: Tsx
severity: warning
message: "forge:typescript/no-dynamic-regexp A RegExp built from a non-literal pattern (new RegExp(input), RegExp(`^${p}`)) escapes it with RegExp.escape() (ES2025, Node 24) unless the text is meant as a pattern: unescaped input changes what matches and can backtrack for ever."
files:
  - packages/core/**
rule:
  any:
    - pattern: new RegExp($A)
    - pattern: new RegExp($A, $$$)
    - pattern: RegExp($A)
    - pattern: RegExp($A, $$$)
constraints:
  A:
    not:
      any:
        - kind: string
        - kind: template_string
          not:
            has:
              kind: template_substitution
              not:
                has:
                  pattern: RegExp.escape($$$)
        - pattern: RegExp.escape($$$)

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/typescript/no-hardcoded-session-secret.yml
# Generated by forge from typescript/no-hardcoded-session-secret (mode: forbid).
id: typescript/no-hardcoded-session-secret
language: Tsx
severity: error
message: forge:typescript/no-hardcoded-session-secret No string literal as a signing secret (express-session, cookie-parser, better-auth, hono/jwt, jsonwebtoken sign/verify, @fastify/cookie, @fastify/session). Read it from the environment or a secret store; a secret in the code signs every session for whoever reads the repository.
files:
  - packages/core/**
ignores:
  - packages/core/**/*.test.*
  - packages/core/**/*.spec.*
  - packages/core/**/__tests__/**
  - packages/core/e2e/**
rule:
  kind: call_expression
  any:
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            pattern: $OPTS
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild: 1
              matches: literal-secret-option
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            kind: member_expression
            has:
              field: property
              regex: ^register$
        - has:
            field: arguments
            all:
              - has:
                  nthChild: 1
                  pattern: $PLUGIN
              - has:
                  nthChild: 2
                  matches: literal-secret-option
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            pattern: $JWT
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild: 2
              matches: literal
    - all:
        - has:
            field: function
            pattern: $COOKIES
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild: 1
              matches: literal
utils:
  literal:
    any:
      - kind: string
      - kind: template_string
        not:
          has:
            kind: template_substitution
      - kind: array
        has:
          any:
            - kind: string
            - kind: template_string
              not:
                has:
                  kind: template_substitution
  literal-secret-option:
    kind: object
    has:
      kind: pair
      all:
        - has:
            field: key
            regex: ^["']?secret["']?$
        - has:
            field: value
            matches: literal
metadata:
  forge_where:
    OPTS:
      declared:
        - package: express-session
          name: session
        - package: better-auth
          name: betterAuth
        - package: hono
          name: jwt
    PLUGIN:
      declared:
        package:
          - "@fastify/cookie"
          - "@fastify/session"
    JWT:
      declared:
        - package: jsonwebtoken
          name:
            - sign
            - verify
        - package: hono
          name:
            - sign
            - verify
    COOKIES:
      declared:
        package: cookie-parser

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/typescript/no-html-sinks.yml
# Generated by forge from typescript/no-html-sinks (mode: forbid).
id: typescript/no-html-sinks
language: Tsx
severity: error
message: "forge:typescript/no-html-sinks No HTML built from a value written into the DOM (XSS): no innerHTML or outerHTML assigned anything but a constant string, and no insertAdjacentHTML, document.write, writeln, createContextualFragment or setHTMLUnsafe whose HTML argument is not constant. Set textContent, build elements, or sanitise in one place."
files:
  - packages/core/**
rule:
  any:
    - kind: assignment_expression
      all:
        - has:
            field: left
            kind: member_expression
            all:
              - has:
                  field: property
                  regex: ^(innerHTML|outerHTML)$
              - has:
                  field: object
                  pattern: $E
        - not:
            has:
              field: right
              any:
                - kind: string
                - kind: template_string
                  not:
                    has:
                      kind: template_substitution
    - kind: call_expression
      all:
        - has:
            field: function
            kind: member_expression
            all:
              - has:
                  field: property
                  regex: ^(insertAdjacentHTML|write|writeln|createContextualFragment|setHTMLUnsafe)$
              - has:
                  field: object
                  pattern: $E
        - has:
            field: arguments
            has:
              nthChild:
                position: 1
                reverse: true
              not:
                any:
                  - kind: string
                  - kind: template_string
                    not:
                      has:
                        kind: template_substitution
metadata:
  forge_where:
    E:
      type:
        package: typescript
        name:
          - Element
          - Document
          - Range
          - ShadowRoot

===== .forge/ast-grep/rules/typescript/no-object-literal-assertion.yml
# Generated by forge from typescript/no-object-literal-assertion (mode: forbid).
id: typescript/no-object-literal-assertion
language: Tsx
severity: error
message: forge:typescript/no-object-literal-assertion No type assertion on an object or array literal ({ … } as T, [x] as T[]); it hides missing and misspelled fields. Annotate the variable, use satisfies T, or pass a type argument; as const and an empty [] are fine.
